Slice 087, `ok-exit` of a step and the hint for a `roc check|build|test` step that exits with 2 (entry `commands`): R-RUN1, R-RUN5, R-RUN7, R-RUN11, R-RUN18, R-RUN19, R-RUN3, R-RUN6, R-RC1 (exit 2 is warnings only), R-E1, R-E4.
One home with the compiler `nightly-2026-10-14-38a3029` installed (as `rn2-words`). `p1/main.roc` pins it, so each `roc` step goes through the proxy to that compiler. The fake runs no child: `fx/exec` gives the end of the child by a needle of the argv (`--output=bad` 1; `--sig` and `tool-sig` the signal 2 (`signal:2`, `Signaled(2)`, slice 087); `roc build main.roc`, `roc check main.roc`, `roc run main.roc`, `roc main.roc`, `scripts/notes.roc` and `tool-two` 2; else 0).
`p2/talon.toml` has a bad `ok-exit` (`[2, 256]`) on the second step of the script `bad`, so each run in `p2` stops before the first step.

| Run | Words | Result | Rules |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | `run okb` in `p1` | `{ run = "roc build main.roc", ok-exit = [2] }` exits with 2: the step passes, one note `tln: note: step "roc build main.roc" exited with 2; this is accepted as success by the ok-exit of the step` on stderr, the next step `tool-next` runs (`exec_in` in `calls.log`), exit 0 | R-RUN18, R-RUN5, R-RUN7, R-RUN1 |
| 2 | `run warnb` in `p1` | `roc build main.roc` (no `ok-exit`) exits with 2: the script stops (`tool-never` does not run), exit 2, the hint of R-RUN19 on stderr | R-RUN19, R-RUN7, R-RUN5, R-E1 |
